@startuml 08-sequence-customer-service
title customer-service - Diagrama de secuencia

skinparam shadowing false
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center

actor "Cliente / Empleado\n(Postman)" as User
participant "CustomerController\n(adaptador WebFlux)" as Controller
participant "CustomerApplicationService\n(casos de uso, RxJava 3)" as Service
participant "CustomerRepositoryPort\n+ adaptador R2DBC" as Repo
database "PostgreSQL\ncustomer_db" as DB
participant "CorrelationIdWebFilter\n(WebFilter, prioridad máxima)" as Correlation

note over User, Correlation
  Todas las solicitudes siguientes atraviesan este filtro antes del controlador.
  Reutiliza X-Correlation-ID si no está vacío; si falta o está en blanco,
  genera un UUID. Todas las respuestas incluyen X-Correlation-ID: {id}
  con el mismo valor recibido o generado.
end note

== 1. Crear cliente (POST /api/v1/customers) ==
User -> Controller : POST /api/v1/customers\nCustomerRequest\nX-Correlation-ID: {id} (opcional)
Controller -> Service : create(command)
Service -> Repo : existsByDocument(documentType, documentNumber)
Repo -> DB : SELECT EXISTS(...)
DB --> Repo : existe / no existe
Repo --> Service : Single<Boolean>
alt documento duplicado
  Service --> Controller : Single.error(DuplicateCustomerDocumentException)
  Controller --> User : 409 Conflict\napplication/problem+json\nX-Correlation-ID: {id}
else documento disponible
  Service -> Repo : save(Customer con status ACTIVE)
  Repo -> DB : INSERT customer
  alt colisión concurrente de documento
    DB --> Repo : violación de restricción única
    Repo --> Service : DuplicateCustomerDocumentException
    Service --> Controller : Single.error(...)
      Controller --> User : 409 Conflict\napplication/problem+json\nX-Correlation-ID: {id}
  else guardado
    DB --> Repo : fila creada
    Repo --> Service : Single<Customer>
    Controller -> Controller : RxJava3Adapter.singleToMono(...)
      Controller --> User : 201 Created + Location\nCustomer\nX-Correlation-ID: {id}
  end
end

== 2. Listar clientes (GET /api/v1/customers) ==
User -> Controller : GET /api/v1/customers\n?customerType&status&page&size\nX-Correlation-ID: {id} (opcional)
Controller -> Service : findAll(customerType, status, page, size)
note right of Service
  status admite ACTIVE, INACTIVE o ALL;
  si se omite, se usa ACTIVE.
  page/size tienen valores predeterminados
  0/20 y size máximo 100.
end note
Service -> Repo : findAll(filtros, página, tamaño)
Repo -> DB : SELECT ... ORDER BY createdAt, id\nLIMIT/OFFSET
DB --> Repo : filas
Repo --> Service : Flowable<Customer>
Controller -> Controller : RxJava3Adapter.flowableToFlux(...)
Controller --> User : 200 OK\napplication/json (arreglo) o application/x-ndjson\nX-Correlation-ID: {id}

== 3. Consultar cliente (GET /api/v1/customers/{customerId}) ==
User -> Controller : GET /api/v1/customers/{customerId}\nX-Correlation-ID: {id} (opcional)
Controller -> Service : findById(customerId)
Service -> Repo : findById(customerId)
Repo -> DB : SELECT customer
DB --> Repo : fila o vacío
Repo --> Service : Single<Customer> / vacío
alt no existe o está INACTIVE
  Service --> Controller : Single.error(CustomerNotFoundException)
  Controller --> User : 404 Not Found\napplication/problem+json\nX-Correlation-ID: {id}
else está ACTIVE
  Controller -> Controller : RxJava3Adapter.singleToMono(...)
  Controller --> User : 200 OK\nCustomer\nX-Correlation-ID: {id}
end

== 4. Actualizar cliente (PUT /api/v1/customers/{customerId}) ==
User -> Controller : PUT /api/v1/customers/{customerId}\nCustomerUpdateRequest\nX-Correlation-ID: {id} (opcional)
Controller -> Service : update(customerId, command)
Service -> Repo : findById(customerId)
Repo -> DB : SELECT customer
DB --> Repo : cliente activo
Repo --> Service : Single<Customer>
Service -> Service : validar campos editables;\nconservar customerType
Service -> Repo : save(customer.update(...))
Repo -> DB : UPDATE customer
DB --> Repo : fila actualizada
Repo --> Service : Single<Customer>
Controller -> Controller : RxJava3Adapter.singleToMono(...)
Controller --> User : 200 OK + Customer\nX-Correlation-ID: {id}
note over Controller, User
  Solicitud inválida: 400.
  Cliente inexistente o INACTIVE: 404.
end note

== 5. Baja lógica (DELETE /api/v1/customers/{customerId}) ==
User -> Controller : DELETE /api/v1/customers/{customerId}\nX-Correlation-ID: {id} (opcional)
Controller -> Service : delete(customerId)
Service -> Repo : findById(customerId)
Repo -> DB : SELECT customer
DB --> Repo : fila o vacío
Repo --> Service : Single<Customer> / vacío
alt no existe o está INACTIVE
  Service --> Controller : error CustomerNotFoundException
  Controller --> User : 404 Not Found\napplication/problem+json\nX-Correlation-ID: {id}
else existe y está ACTIVE
  Service -> Repo : save(customer.deactivate())
  Repo -> DB : UPDATE status = INACTIVE
  DB --> Repo : OK
  Repo --> Service : Single<Customer>
  Controller -> Controller : RxJava3Adapter.completableToMono(...)
  Controller --> User : 204 No Content\nX-Correlation-ID: {id}
end

== 6. Reactivar cliente (PATCH /api/v1/customers/{customerId}/activate) ==
User -> Controller : PATCH /api/v1/customers/{customerId}/activate\nX-Correlation-ID: {id} (opcional)
Controller -> Service : activate(customerId)
Service -> Repo : findById(customerId)
Repo -> DB : SELECT customer
DB --> Repo : fila o vacío
Repo --> Service : Single<Customer> / vacío
alt no existe
  Service --> Controller : error CustomerNotFoundException
  Controller --> User : 404 Not Found\napplication/problem+json\nX-Correlation-ID: {id}
else existe
  Service -> Repo : save(customer.activate())
  Repo -> DB : UPDATE status = ACTIVE
  DB --> Repo : fila actualizada
  Repo --> Service : Single<Customer>
  Controller -> Controller : RxJava3Adapter.singleToMono(...)
  Controller --> User : 200 OK + Customer\nX-Correlation-ID: {id}
end

@enduml
